Relations between Sanyan and Balisca began with the rise of the [[Maroon Confederacy]], as Sanyan under the leadership of [[Nsuukidem Jesumbo]] to fund the [[Maroon pirates]] that were working to disrupt the [[Kaftian slave trade]]. Relations between the two states were solidified with the [[Kafto-Ethiopian Charter]], a pact of mutual support on both sides of the [[Ethiopian Ocean]]. Following the [[Volisanya Boba]] period and the [[Baliscan War of Independence|establishment]] of the [[Northern Confederation]], the countries exchanged diplomatic recognition.

The Maroon Confederacy later intervened in the [[Baliscan Civil War]], playing a decisive role in beating back the [[Siege of Castejón]], and in subsequent years developed an amiable relationship with [[Anyos Federales|Reconstructionist Balisca]], which recognized the Kafto-Ethiopian Charter. The Confederacy continued to exercise sovereignty until it confederated with the Baliscan Confederation at the [[1883 Confederal Convention]], from which the Balisca assumed all obligations of the Charter.
|}

=== Abyala ===
