|'''{{flag|Asikyira}}'''||1823||See [[Asikyira–Balisca relations]]

Asikyira and Balisca are neighboring countries in [[Abyala]], and share close political, economic and cultural ties. The singularity of the bilateral relationship between the two countries originates from a strong historical connection, stemming from Illypnian colonization in the 16th century.

Balisca was, in 1822, the first country to recognize the [[independence of Asikyira]], immediately after the Declaration of Independence. Balisca and Asikyira were the only Abyalan nations to send troops to fight in Kaftia alongside the Allies in the [[Great Adonian War]]. The relationship between both countries represents the two most populated and powerful countries in Abyala; due to the political and economic weight of both countries in the [[Western Hemisphere]].

Bilateral relations show a history of competition between the two countries. Balisca and Asikyira have avoided direct armed conflict, despite several periods of tense relations.
|}

